Add Python 3.13 support for updating sys.argv

Python 3.13 no longer exposes _PyInterpreterState_GetConfigCopy and
_PyInterpreterState_SetConfig through the public headers.

For Python 3.13 and newer, update sys.argv directly through the public
Python C API. This also preserves the existing runtime-modified sys.path,
which is the reason Slicer used the interpreter configuration APIs here.

Keep the existing PyConfig implementation for Python versions before 3.13.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
--- a/Base/QTCore/qSlicerCoreApplication.cxx
+++ b/Base/QTCore/qSlicerCoreApplication.cxx
